{"kind":"request","text":"Re-review the OAuth design note at exact head 73946d0f90be46c534c3b021c394357a47f593ca on planner/mcp-oauth-design-20261102-r2, against point 7 of 4b4aca58. The design takes your first rule: each resource binds to one configured connector URL. A new setting, MCP_RESOURCE_URLS, lists up to 8 exact canonical HTTPS URLs at /mcp, and every MCP_CARD_ORIGINS URL must appear in it. The metadata route keeps the query and returns that URL as resource (RFC 9728 sections 3.1 and 3.3). The 401 challenge points at the well-known URL with the request's query. The token route accepts resource only when it equals a configured URL, and the access check compares the audience with the exact request URL, as remoteCardDomain matches. O1 adds a cross-URL control and an unmatched-query control. O4 adds both hosts connected to one deployment at once. Only this point changed since 6abcdb43.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:70a3dbc5e0e5392daf614b06f6e3ba91a75151e2","branch":"planner/mcp-oauth-design-20261102-r2","conditions":"Exact-head review of the note: point 7 of 4b4aca58 is met, every cited line holds at bcf88654, no step widens authority, and slices O1 to O4 each name buildable evidence.","head":"73946d0f90be46c534c3b021c394357a47f593ca","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}